Hi

My original question :
> I have just did a fresh installation of my alpha2100 server model 4/200 
> to OSF1 v3.2 on the system disk rz0.  Previously, I have data on my rz2c 
> disk.  The previous domain on the rz2c disk is usenetdom and the fileset 
> in this domain is news.  The filesystem mounted on usenetdom#news is 
> /var/spool/news.  May I know how can I re-mount back this /var/spool/news 
> filesystem so that I can get back the data on the rz2c disk.

Summary:
mkdir /etc/fdmns/usenetdom
cd /etc/fdmns/usenetdom
ln -s /dev/rz2c
mount usenetdom#news /var/spool/news

Remember: Do NOT do a mkfdmn, it will destroy things for you.

	Morten

