The Original Problem was :

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hi, I am running OSF/1 3.0 and changed the security to enhanced.  One of the
accounts , can't login , telling him account changed by root, (as I changed the
password for him the first time he couldn't login), then it tells him that
account is disabled .  I couldn't solve this problem , and it doesn't make sense
to drop the user (or remove him) then create him again .

Any Suggestions ? 

Thanks in advance . 

Deya

---------------------------  E N D    O F   O R I G I N A L   M E S S A G E  --------------------------


The problem is solved,in a very simple way, it seems that when you change security , some accounts
(may be they don't match some criteria in the C2 or whatever..) get disabled .

A summary of the solution :

You need to run the /usr/tcb/bin/XIsso program, from the console
 (or X-windows capable display).  You then select "modify user accounts"
 and select the user from the menu-box next to the username field
 at the top of the form.  Once the user account information is displayed,
 look at the bottom of the form.  There is a button for 'account disabled'. 
 Toggle this back off.  That's it. 


